<title>USA: Central U.S. carlot pork at 1500 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>Central U.S. carlot pork at 1500 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compared with Monday's close, fresh loins were steady to $2.00 lower; butts were firm; skinned hams 17-20 lbs held steady; 20-26 lbs $1.00 to $2.00 lower; seedless bellies $1.00 to $2.00 higher; lean trimmings $1.00 to $2.00 lower. - USDA</p>
<p>Trading was slow, with light demand and light to moderate offerings</p>
